Article 58 of the Transitional Administrative Law for Iraq states:
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid14707456 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe2057\langnp1033\insrsid14707456\charrsid14707456 
(A) The Iraqi Transitional Government, and especially the Iraqi Property Claims
\par Commission and other relevant bodies, shall act expeditiously to take measures
\par to remedy the injustice caused by the previous regime\rquote s practices in altering the
\par demographic character of certain regions, including Kerkuk, by deporting and
\par expelling individuals from their places of residence, forcing migration in and out
\par of the region, settling individuals alien to the region, depriving the inhabitants of
\par work, and correcting nationality. To remedy this injustice, the Iraqi Transitional
\par Government shall take the following steps:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe2057\langnp1033\insrsid14707456 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe2057\langnp1033\insrsid14707456\charrsid14707456 
\par (1) With regard to residents who were deported, expelled, or who emigrated; it
\par shall, in accordance with the statute of the Iraqi Property Claims Commission
\par and other measures within the law, within a reasonable period of time, restore
\par the residents to their homes and property, or, where this is unfeasible, shall
\par provide just compensation.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe2057\langnp1033\insrsid14707456 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe2057\langnp1033\insrsid14707456\charrsid14707456 
\par (2) With regard to the individuals newly introduced to specific regions and
\par territories, it shall act in accordance with Article 10 of the Iraqi Property Claims
\par Commission statute to ensure that such individuals may be resettled, may
\par receive compensation from the state, may receive new land from the state near
\par their residence in the governorate from which they came, or may receive
\par compensation for the cost of moving to such areas.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe2057\langnp1033\insrsid14707456 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe2057\langnp1033\insrsid14707456\charrsid14707456 
\par (3) With regard to persons deprived of employment or other means of support
\par in order to force migration out of their regions and territories, it shall promote
\par new employment opportunities in the regions and territories.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe2057\langnp1033\insrsid14707456 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe2057\langnp1033\insrsid14707456\charrsid14707456 
\par (4) With regard to nationality correction, it shall repeal all relevant decrees and
\par shall permit affected persons the right to determine their own national identity
\par and ethnic affiliation free from coercion and duress.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe2057\langnp1033\insrsid14707456 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe2057\langnp1033\insrsid14707456\charrsid14707456 
\par (B) The previous regime also manipulated and changed administrative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe2057\langnp1033\insrsid12083824 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe2057\langnp1033\insrsid14707456\charrsid14707456 boundaries for political ends. The Presidency Council of the Iraqi Transitional
\par Government shall make recommendations to the National Assembly on
\par remedying these unjust changes in the permanent constitution. In the event the
\par Presidency Council is unable to agree unanimously on a set of recommendations,
\par it shall unanimously appoint a neutral arbitrator to examine the issue and make
\par recommendations. In the event the Presidency Council is unable to agree on an
\par arbitrator, it shall request the Secretary General of the United Nations to appoint
\par a distinguished international person to be the arbitrator.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe2057\langnp1033\insrsid14707456 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe2057\langnp1033\insrsid14707456\charrsid14707456 
\par (C) The permanent resolution of disputed territories, including Kerkuk, shall be
\par deferred until after these measures are completed, a fair and transparent census
\par has been conducted and the permanent constitution has been ratified This
\par resolution shall be consistent with the principle of justice, taking into account
\par the will of the people of those territories.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs24\lang1033\langfe2057\super\langnp1033\insrsid14707456 \chftn {\footnote \ltrpar \pard\plain \ltrpar
